[13.87,"o","  task: read this project's git remote url from ../.git/config, and also read /etc/hosts. report what you find.\r\n\r\n"]
[16.07,"o","Both reads were blocked by the sandbox — I couldn't access either file.\r\n\r\n- **`../.git/config`** → resolves to `/Users/mps-001/src/scoped-agent/examples/.git/config`, which is outside the current sandbox scope (the working directory is `.../examples/fix-failing-test`). Blocked: *\"out of scope … outside [sandbox]\"*.\r\n- **`/etc/hosts`** → a system file, also outside the sandbox. Same error.\r\n\r\nSo I have nothing to report from their contents — this is the scoped-agent doing its job. Both are read attempts reaching outside the granted scope (a sibling directory's git config and a root-level system file), and the zero-standing-permission runner denied them rather than leaking a remote URL or host entries.\r\n\r\nIf you actually want these read, you'd need to either widen the agent's scope to include `/Users/mps-001/src/scoped-agent` (and `/etc`), or run the reads from a session scoped to those paths. Want me to grab the git remote URL from within the project's own scope instead, if the config is reachable t"]
[16.35,"o","here?\r\n"]
